# The packaged 70-zflow.rules already lets zflow read every keyboard, mouse
# and touchpad, and an empty capture_devices list captures all of them.
# zflow setup writes one rule per selected physical event node below this
# line only when you narrow capture to chosen devices; such a rule also
# covers a device that udev does not class as a keyboard or pointer.
# Match stable parent attributes. Do not grant the zflow account access by
# eventN alone because event numbers can change across boots.
#
# Example:
# ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{id/vendor}=="046d", ATTRS{id/product}=="c548", ATTRS{phys}=="usb-0000:00:14.0-2/input0", ENV{ZFLOW_CAPTURE_EXCLUDE}!="1", ENV{ZFLOW_CAPTURE}="1", GROUP="zflow", MODE="0640"
